  "source": "pragma cashscript ^0.14.0;\n\n// =====================================================================================\n// Evermore Arena: holds every ghost (39 B 'G' commitments). A ghost is the copy of a hero\n// that other players challenge; its owner is paid on every challenge without being online.\n//\n// Only path, fight(): a lane of the game category (minting capability) is input 0, and the\n// ghost comes back to this same address at the SAME index, still in the category, still a\n// ghost with the same id ('G' + id preserved), value kept. The lane function at input 0\n// pins the rest of the commitment (defences + 1, beaten + 1, or the level up refresh).\n//\n// Stops:\n// - spending a ghost without the referee: no lane at input 0 -> fails.\n// - burning a ghost by slipping it into a lane path that does not expect it: every lane\n//   path pins every output index, so the output at this ghost's index is not a ghost with\n//   its id -> fails (tested for raise and challenge).\n// - swapping one ghost for another, or moving it off the Arena.\n// No owner path and no burn path: a ghost lives as long as the chain does.\n// =====================================================================================\ncontract Arena(bytes32 gameCategory) {\n    function fight() {\n        require(tx.inputs[0].tokenCategory == gameCategory + 0x02);\n        int i = this.activeInputIndex;\n        require(tx.outputs[i].lockingBytecode == tx.inputs[i].lockingBytecode);\n        require(tx.outputs[i].tokenCategory == gameCategory);\n        require(tx.outputs[i].nftCommitment.split(5)[0] == tx.inputs[i].nftCommitment.split(5)[0]);\n        require(tx.outputs[i].value >= tx.inputs[i].value);\n    }\n}\n",
